k on the gateway (ledger: 85kâ€“1.98M cache_read tokens). **Fixed + live-verified** (truthful per-turn cost, real model/tier, cache-hit%); see `PLAN-Reporting-Accuracy-2026-05-27.md`.\n- **The real cost/latency driver is the within-turn agentic tool-loop**, which OpenClaw cannot tier per step (it fixes one model per run) and whose framework overhead (~8.6s warm; auth + per-turn tool-registry rebuild) is large. SDK spikes: no stable `executeTool` (OpenClaw is an MCP *client*); `subagent.run` is the only stable way to reuse OpenClaw's stateful tools; `ownsCompaction:true` fires per-iteration compaction on the gateway path.\n- **Convergence (mine + two external efforts):** build a **Sovereign t2r Harness** â€” a custom loop the agent fully owns, running a **recursive t2r cycle at every ReAct step** (the validated gold standard, `GOLD-STANDARD-T2R-Recursive-Agentic-Loop.md`). **Key correction:** do NOT swap *remote* reasoning models mid-loop (cross-model cache cold-start = measured **+120â€“242%**); win instead via free-local observation **compression** + **local sub-decisions ($0)** + **one cache-stable remote model per loop**.\n- **Final spec:** `REPORT-Sovereign-t2r-Harness-Gold-Standard-FINAL.md` â€” per-agent **Soul** (cache-stable file), **persistent 3-tier memory** (episodic/semantic/procedural, written by free local models, retrieved into the message tail), **tiered tools** (basic in-harness via off-the-shelf MCP; complex/stateful delegated to OpenClaw via `subagent.run`, migrated in over time).\n- **G-Brain reframe (the strategy change vs the v5 headline):** GBrain is installed but is **demoted from \"the agent layer\" to a deferred, offline training flywheel** that distills the harness's own cheap local tier from the `g27-v3` envelopes the harness emits â€” **never in the per-turn hot loop** (Bun-leak rule). v5 planned to borrow GBrain wholesale *as* the agent layer; the convergence builds our own sovereign agent layer instead and keeps GBrain for what it's uniquely good at (offline LoRA/distillation).\n\n**Decision:** go directly to Phase 2 (build the Sovereign t2r Harness). Next artifact: the module-by-module software plan. Session log: `SESSION-LOG-2026-05-27-t2r-harness-convergence.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The v4 â†’ v5 reframe (load-bearing)\n\n**Status:** locked\n\nv4 mostly designed a *brain*. The tasteâ†’reasoning architecture, the cognitive cells, the plasticity catalog (26 mutations across 5 layers â€” not v4's prose-claimed 17), the curriculum-driven training, the adjudicator and its training tuples, the distillation losses, the drift detection â€” all of it is *cognition substrate*. v4 calls this work \"the path to production\" but production of *what* was hand-waved: the same plan also gestures at clusters of W/S/Math agents using the brain, but never separated the agent layer from the brain layer.\n\n**The single deepest cut in this review (Retro Entry 1 â†’ Entry 14):** brain â‰  agent. The agent is the persistent operating unit that *uses* a brain to do work â€” it has its own memory, skills, tools, planning loop, quality-signal pipeline, and ongoing identity. v4 fused the two; v5 pries them apart.\n\nThree corollaries flow from the reframe:\n\n1. **The agent layer is commoditized; the GWL brain is the moat.** Anthropic, Google, OpenAI, and a dozen frameworks (LangGraph, Letta, CrewAI, AutoGen, Cowork, Claude Code) have collectively spent hundreds of engineer-years on the agent layer. GWL needs *best-in-class* at this layer but does not need to be *innovative* here. The tasteâ†’reasoning brain, the cognitive cell substrate, the in-harness brain-training pipeline â€” those are differentiated and worth defending. Everything else: borrow.\n2. **GBrain (Garry Tan's, MIT, 11.1kâ˜…, OpenClaw-native, released 2026-04-05) delivers ~80% of v0's agent-layer scope** in a 30-minute install. 29 baseline skills + Git-versioned markdown Brain Repo + pgvector retrieval + dream cycle + entity-tier escalation + `skillify` workflow + `Minions` job queue + MCP server. GBrain is purpose-built for the runtime John has chosen and is open-source under terms compatible with this workspace. **Adopting GBrain replaces months of v4-implied build-effort at the agent layer.**\n3. **GBrain does NOT deliver the quality-signal capture loop.** No skill success-rate scoring, no Wilson-CI tournaments at the agent layer, no RLHF/DPO, no 5-flavor signals (outcome / user / resource / self-consistency / replay). This is *the* v5 GWL addition: hook-layer instrumentation at GBrain's skill and dream-cycle boundaries that captures the five signals and feeds them into both the GWL brain-training pipeline AND GBrain's skill-improvement workflow.\n\nThe clean way to say what v5 *is*: **assemble best-in-class agent-layer commodity beneath a GWL t2r brain, instrument the seam with quality-signal hooks, and use the result for daily work while the brain continues to deepen underneath.**\n\n---\n\n## 2. Current state recap\n\n**Status:** locked (consumed from STATE-OF-PROJECT-2026-05-13; tooling additions through 2026-05-14)\n\n### Brain layer (v4's territory) â€” substantially advanced\n\nWave 7 closed across three phases on 2026-05-08/09. Test gate moved 315 â†’ 374 â†’ 442 â†’ **498/498/0/0**. All scoped Wave-7 gaps closed: G-24 integrator-fuse, G-25 best-in-class skills, G-26 distillation losses, G-27 training-capture envelope, G-28 skill-evolution disabled-shell (gated off in Phase B), G-29 replay scheduler, G-31 drift-judge expert, G-32 adjudicator-tuple corpus. The Adjudicator-training-tuple corpus has been accumulating since 2026-05-08 â€” 5+ days of real capture data.\n\nPlasticity catalog landed 2026-05-07 (Session 6: 26 mutation IDs across 5 layers, despite v4 prose saying 17). Plasticity proposer skeleton landed 2026-05-07 (Session 7).\n\nPhase A foundations shipped 2026-05-07 (alpha-linear and alpha-lorentz pilot duo, SOULs at STRICT parity, per-agent page route, Phase B plan committed with `eng-1-9` u01-u03 unit slice locked). Linux smoke green; Windows smoke not yet confirmed.\n\nCURR-1 audit tool shipped 2026-05-07 (`audit-completeness.py`, 18 tests). The cp1252 / curly-quotes bug that ate the first audit pass is now fixed.\n\nPhase B first GLCI cadence ran 2026-05-07 evening (baseline 4/6 on both pilots, threshold 0.85).\n\n### Hardware â€” better than v4 anticipated\n\nHost migrated laptop â†’ **gwl-server** on 2026-05-12. Dell XPS 8960, i9-13900K (24c/32t), 32 GB DDR5 (single-DIMM punch-list item: matched second stick ~$80-100), RTX 4070 12 GB Ada, 1.8 TB OS NVMe + 1.9 TB workspace NVMe. Tailscale-served at `https://gwl.tailb49f65.ts.net`. **v4's INFRA-1 cloud-VM plan is moot** â€” the 12 GB VRAM on the 4070 caps Phase C at QLoRA on â‰¤8B students, which is exactly the design target for the local-distillation workstream.\n\nPhase C Step A scripts authored 2026-05-13 (paused per John's request, not blocking v5): `Install-Phase-C-Stack.ps1` + `smoke_qlora.py`. Decisions locked: Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct + Miniconda + Python 3.12 + cu130 wheels + D:\\ for venv & weights.\n\n### Agent layer (v5's territory) â€” paper, but two enablers landed today\n\n`alpha` exists as an OpenClaw agent (Gemini-backed, 5 skills, sub-30s `hi` response after the 2026-04-30 recovery). `prime-coder` and `sigma` are operational. **Everything else in the agent registry is paper** â€” W/S/Math clusters are persona files, no spawned worker agent has run. The \"cluster operation\" v4 promised has not begun.\n\n`project-manager-kit` shipped 2026-05-07 and evolved substantially on 2026-05-13 during the anchor-coach pilot. Real-Intent Protocol (Parable of the Oranges) + Run-don't-narrate + use-claude-code skill + nine other T1/T2/T3 edits landed. Canonical relocated to `C:\\dev\\Project-Manager\\`; the Agentic-Home copy needs a one-way-sync resolution in S1.\n\n**Two enablers landed today (2026-05-14) that change v5 viability:**\n\n- **`expert-coder-Win11` skill shipped** â€” SKILL.md + 8 references + `Test-Win11Environment.ps1` (now bridge-aware after a real-host verification bug-fix this session) + CRITIQUE-PASS-1.md. All five mirror locations match by MD5 (canonical `C:\\dev\\Expert-Coder-Win11\\`, `skills-master\\`, `.claude\\skills\\`, `.gemini\\skills\\`, `~\\.openclaw\\skills\\`). Alpha and Prime Coder personas updated. Memory entry `skill_windows_coding` committed. Bootstrap auto-discovery confirmed (line 134 of Bootstrap-Agentic-Home.ps1 picks up any `skills-master\\<name>\\SKILL.md` without explicit reference).\n- **Coworkâ†”host PowerShell bridge is LIVE** (`mcp__Claude_Code_Bridge__run_command`). Destructive-op gating + admin-elevation flagging built in. Eliminates the paste-prompt failure mode the V5-RETRO flagged as the existential risk to execution time. Every v5 sprint task can now write *and run* host scripts directly.\n\nTogether these two reduce v5's \"what could go wrong at the Windows host\" risk class materially. Most Â§4 S1 tasks below assume the bridge is available; if it were not, S1 would need ~30% more elapsed time.\n\n### What this means for v5 sequencing\n\nThe brain layer has more than enough runway to start v0 right now without further brain work. The brain work *should continue in parallel* (the in-harness corpus that v0 produces is the input to the next brain-training cycle), but it does not gate v0. **The bottleneck is agent-layer work, not brain-layer work.**\n\n---\n\n## 3. The v0 / v1 / v2 spec table\n\n**Status:** locked (consumed from Retro Entry 15-18; walkthrough-confirmed with John 2026-05-14)\n\nThe critical path is one agent's ladder, not a phase-cluster arc. Specialization (cluster operation, W/S/Math agents) happens *after* v0 is in daily use.\n\n| Version | Agent layer | Brain layer | Sleep updates | Wallet (revised) | Gate to promote |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **v0** | OpenClaw runtime + GBrain (Tan's, v0.19+) on top with native `AGENTS.md` resolver at workspace root, t2r dispatcher as a brain-layer module GBrain calls. Best-in-class skill bundle (see Â§4). **Cowork-comparable for John's daily use.** Vehicle is the **`alpha-v0`** agent (shipped 2026-05-16 commits `6250cf5a` + `6482d06d`; separate tile and routing entry from the legacy `alpha` agent which still routes to the brain-research v2 orchestrator). In addition to alpha-v0 (the general-purpose vehicle), the v0 architecture supports **v0 specialists** â€” sibling agents with a different skill bundle + persona prompt + optional default project binding. Same dispatcher, same model defaults, same wallet. See Â§13 for the workstream cadence and Â§4 S2/S3 for the rollout. | t2r architecture: two sequential frontier calls per turn. Taste first (curate + sharp-query + skill/resource hint), then reasoning (execute against the curated context). No cognitive cells yet, no local LLMs. **Both halves top-tier frontier** â€” default **Gemini Pro both**, with **Anthropic Opus** available per-agent / per-turn for high-value escalation. Smart cheap/expensive routing is a v1+ capability, not v0. | Agent skills (success-rate scoring, retire low-performers â€” **human-in-loop through v0, no auto-retire**; aligns with GBrain's stated \"human-stays-in-the-loop\" philosophy), tools (usage stats, capability ranking), hooks (threshold tuning from outcomes). **No brain-side training in v0** â€” both halves are frontier-driven. | **$100/month per active agent** (soft alert at $80, hard cap enforced at the dispatcher with graceful-degrade + interactive cap-override). **Scope: measures t2r dispatcher calls only.** GBrain's internal LLM + embedding usage is a *separate* line item (see \"GBrain operational wallet\" note below the table). Cowork reference: $200/mo flat. **Revision triggers:** first soft-alert hit, OR end of S1 review, OR John reports cap is friction. Revision = `routing.json` commit + log entry in `logs/wallet-revisions.jsonl`. **Precedence:** raise the wallet, do not downgrade models. | **Per-workflow-type adoption matrix** (code / research / drafting / finance / trip-planning / project-management each tracked separately) replaces binary \"is John using it.\" Promotion to v1 = â‰¥3 workflow types showing â‰¥50% v0 adoption with stable signal quality. |\n| **v1** | Same as v0. | t2r with **cognitive cells** for taste-cell and reasoning-cell. Each cell still frontier-driven (no local LLMs). Cell substrate provides MoE-style expert routing inside each half. | Everything v0 sleeps **+** cognitive-cell config (gate residuals, expert routing inside cells, atlas concept reorganization). Still no LoRA â€” brain weights are not changing. | Same as v0 in expectation; cell substrate adds ~10% routing overhead amortized. | Cell substrate stably outperforms v0 on the same trust-ladder tasks for **2 weeks**. Cell-config sleep mutations demonstrably improving metric. |\n| **v2** | Same as v0. | v1 cognitive cells **+** local QLoRA-trained 8B student per cell (taste-student, reasoning-student) on the gwl-server 4070. **Gating function** decides per turn: local student vs frontier escalation. First neural plasticity. | Everything v1 sleeps **+** LoRA on the local students from the in-harness training corpus **+** gating-function calibration (when to escalate). | Wallet shrinks: gating diverts ~40-60% of turns to local students (~$0.001/turn) vs frontier (~$0.01-0.05/turn). Per-agent monthly burn target: **$300-700**. | Local students serve â‰¥40% of turns at â‰¥90% quality parity (measured via held-out frontier-judge). Gating function calibrated (escalates correctly on hard turns). |\n\nAfter v2 works on a single agent, GWL is in position to evaluate the full-brain rollout. After v0 works, **specialization can begin in parallel** with v1/v2 brain deepening â€” W/S/Math clusters as additional v0-shaped agents with specialty skill bundles.","numLines":120,"startLine":1,"totalLines":510}}}
